Same defect class as karr #38, one file over and out of its scope.

IO::K8s::List::kind() (lib/IO/K8s/List.pm:110-117) has two paths:

  1. the first item's ->kind . "List"
  2. a fallback deriving it from item_class: /::(\w+)$/ . "List"

Path 1 is fixed for free by karr #38 (kind() now falls back to the bare
class name). Path 2 still returns undef for a single-segment item_class,
so TO_JSON emits apiVersion but no kind::

  my $l = IO::K8s::List->new(items => [], item_class => "Bare");
  $l->api_version;  # "vendor.example.com/v1"
  $l->kind;         # undef   <-- should be "BareList"

That fallback is exactly what item_class exists for -- the POD says
"Used for empty lists where the type can't be inferred" -- so the gap only
shows on an empty list of a single-segment CRD Kind, which is the case the
attribute was added for.

Fix is the same one-line shape as #38: no "::" means the whole name is the
last segment. Wants a serialization assertion (the emitted list manifest
carries kind:), not just an accessor read.

Found while doing karr #38; left out deliberately because #38 was scoped to
